{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Handoff (session 3d705fec ended before merge)\n\nThe ticket stays in_progress. Remaining work:\n1. Gerrit change 3402 (patch set 1, e0e55946d1252b76cc0740ce9b8cc6965853b8f8, hashtag rebar-session-3d705fec): waiting on LLM-Review and Verified, with neither vote cast at handoff. Submit it with `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py 3402 --revision <current sha>` once both votes are +1 and no comments are unresolved. Worktree: `.rebar/worktrees/win-sweep-6798` (branch win-sweep-6798).\n2. After the merge, run `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main` or wait for the next scheduled run, and confirm that `sweep (windows)` concludes `success`. That run is the evidence for AC5. If the run is red, the red tests are new regressions or intermittent tests outside the 5-run union; add them to the matching class file or file a bug for them.\n3. Tick the AC boxes. AC1 through AC4 are evidenced in the 2026-11-16 comment. Then run verify_completion_start and close with close_class `preexisting` from a worktree fast-forwarded to origin/main.\n\nThe 10 class bugs (halfcrazed-rubbly-whimbrel, citreous-talented-wildebeest, obtuse-phenocryst-verdin, almondy-columned-iguanodon, arctic-unsecular-esok, warmish-primordial-neontetra, injured-reclusive-tamarin, leafy-gorillian-gnat, charitable-tyrannical-hydra, breezy-hogged-mastiff) are open and unclaimed. Each one owns its `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/<class>.args` file. They are not prerequisites for closing this ticket, because its AC5 is met once the subset is held green."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794868280859004574,"uuid":"65e1d49a-7736-4312-9c00-6fe6ed0ee81e"}